\begin{proposition}[The coset defect is infinite]\label{prop:infinite-defect}
Let \(a_*^{-1}(H_t)/H_s\) denote the pointed set of left cosets of \(H_s\) inside \(a_*^{-1}(H_t)\le\pi_1(\Omega_s,z_*)\).  Then the cosets \(\gamma^nH_s\), \(n\in\mathbb Z\), are pairwise distinct; in particular \(a_*^{-1}(H_t)/H_s\) is infinite.
\end{proposition}

\begin{remark}\label{rem:coset-set}
Here \(a_*^{-1}(H_t)/H_s\) is a pointed set of left cosets; it is not asserted to be a quotient group unless normality of \(H_s\) is separately proved.  Any carrier (e.g.\ a ribbon tree) that identifies these cosets to a point hides the analytic obstruction and is not proof-faithful.  The minimal replacement state recorded by the source note is
\[
 \mathfrak S_{\mathrm{loc}}=\bigl(\operatorname{Comp}(F^{-1}B),\ \{\tau(X)\},\ H_s,H_t,\ H_s\backslash\pi_1(\Omega_s),\ a_*^{-1}(H_t)/H_s\bigr).  \tag{9.1}
\]
\end{remark}

\begin{proposition}[Alignment and realization quantifiers]\label{prop:realization}
The statements proved without further hypotheses are precisely the following.
\begin{enumerate}
\item Every first canonical localization of an ordinary primitively \(p\)-renormalizable quadratic polynomial, \(p>1\), has the collision with certificate (6.3).
\item That collision propagates through every pullback depth of that same seed.
\item Whenever that same seed has KL direct-decoration data, the exact direct-decoration maps \(I_{m,n}\), their full universal-cover tile lifts, and their full glued pseudo-piece inclusions are noninjective.
\end{enumerate}
Item (3) is an implication about an aligned realized stage.  It does not infer that an arbitrary abstract canonical seed has a particular decoration.
\end{proposition}

\begin{remark}[Separate realization routes; not used here]\label{rem:realization-routes}
A separate realization statement may be supplied either by
\begin{itemize}
\item a named quadratic parameter whose primitive renormalization straightens to a non-satellite KL decoration germ, or
\item the standard primitive-tuning theorem, applied to a primitive postcritically finite quadratic base and a non-satellite quadratic germ.
\end{itemize}
Until such a realization is source-locked, the present results are not used to change an existential statement about a narrower parameter subclass.  What is settled unconditionally is the behavior of the actual canonical-localization map itself: any proof that treats localization as embedding-preserving is invalid.
\end{remark}

